    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite is Google’s low-latency, cost-focused multimodal Flash-Lite SKU for high-throughput subagent work, document parsing, translation, and simple extraction. The stable Gemini API model code is <code>gemini-3.5-flash-lite</code> (docs updated July 2026). Google announced it on 21 Jul 2026 with Gemini 3.6 Flash and 3.5 Flash Cyber.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />
    <p>Documented on the API model page: text, image, video, audio, and PDF in; text out; 1,048,576 input / 65,536 output tokens; thinking, function calling, code execution, computer use (preview), search and Maps grounding, structured outputs, URL context, caching, file search; Batch / Flex / Priority supported.</p>
    <p>Standard paid pricing on the Gemini Developer API pricing page: <strong>$0.30</strong> per 1M input tokens and <strong>$2.50</strong> per 1M output tokens (including thinking). Free-tier input/output is listed as free of charge.</p>
    <p>Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index (secondary): Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite <strong>22</strong> on the <a href="https://artificialanalysis.ai/leaderboards/models">Artificial Analysis leaderboard</a> (fetched 22 Sep 2026).</p>
    <p>This page is a short stub. Prefer the Flash and Pro cards for full six-heading treatment.</p>
